[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+```[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+`bash -n` on the file confirms the parse error. The script has 351 lines; line 350
 is the last significant line (`tap_index_enroll_team "$WORKTREE"`), but the parse
error indicates an unmatched double-quote detected somewhere earlier that the parse
r can't close.[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+## Suspected cause[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+The script uses two `<<'PY'` heredocs:[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+1. **Lines 138–167** (offline path) — works fine. Simple `if ! python3 ... <<'PY'`
 without wrapping.[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+2. **Lines 203–325** (normal registration path) — **the problematic one**. Wraps t
he python call in a double-quoted command substitution:[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+```bash[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+if ! _write_out="$(python3 -B - ... 2>"$_write_err" <<'PY'[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+...[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+PY[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+)[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+"; then[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+```[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+The pattern `_write_out="$(... <<'PY'\n...\nPY\n)"` — heredoc inside `$()` inside
double-quotes — may be tripping up bash 3.2's parser. The offline path (without the
 `_write_out="$(...)"` wrapper) parses fine.[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+## Verification steps[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+```bash[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+# Confirm parse error[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+bash -n /Users/runner/.hermes/skills/tap/scripts/tap-register.sh[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+# Test that a minimal version of the pattern works in bash 3.2[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+# (heredoc in $() in double-quotes)[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+```[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+## Possible fixes[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+1. **Refactor the `_write_out` capture** to use a temp file instead of `$()` + her
edoc (most robust across bash versions)[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+2. **Use a different heredoc wrapper** (e.g. `<<-PY` with indented terminator, or
avoid the double-quote wrapping)[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+3. **Upgrade bash** to 4+ (unlikely to be acceptable — macOS ships 3.2)[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+4. **Split the Python into a standalone script** and call it without heredoc gymna
stics[39m[49m
[38;5;231m[48;5;22m+[39m[49m
